    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full build passes. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nUnified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single stored `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the derived `checkDigit` field.\n\n**New/renamed logic (single responsibility preserved):**\n- **`MemberIdGenerator`** (replaces `CustomerCodeGenerator`): builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` \u2014 reusing the existing `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone+lastName)` first-8-upper-hex (the region-and-hash identity), `FiscalYear` for the 2-digit FY, and `LuhnCheckDigit` for CHK over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. It keeps the collision-handling (`deduplicate`) and region-extraction responsibilities, now operating on the memberId (region = leading letter run, since FY digits always follow).\n- **`FiscalYear.twoDigit(...)`**: extracted the 2-digit year so both `label()` (\"FY26\") and the memberId (\"26\") share one source of truth.\n- Deleted `CustomerCodeGenerator` and `MembershipNumberFormatter`.\n\n**Wiring updated to reference the unified id:**\n- `Owner`: field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id`.\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.assignMemberId(...)`: now passes the registration date into the generator and dedupes on memberId.\n- `OwnerRepository` + all three impls (Spring Data, JPA, JDBC): `findByCustomerCodeStartingWith` \u2192 `findByMemberIdStartingWith`.\n- `OwnerAuditLogger` audit line and `OwnerCreatedEvent` record: now carry `memberId` (the primary-identifier hook now returns it).\n- `OwnerMapper`: dropped `membershipNumber`/`checkDigit`; `locality`/`timezone`/`ownerSegment` resolve from `memberId` via `LocalityResolver.fromMemberId(...)`; `Owner.memberId` maps straight to the DTO.\n- `openapi.yml`: replaced `customerCode`/`checkDigit`/`membershipNumber` with a `memberId` schema.\n- All four DB schemas: `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id` (widened to VARCHAR(32) to fit the id plus any dedup suffix).\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`. The audit output confirms a real id, e.g. `memberId=NSW2616E6609E3` (region `NSW`, FY `26`, HASH8 `16E6609E`, CHK `3`).",
